{
 "id": "lem-trf-algebraic-space-open-gluing",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Gluing algebraic spaces along open subfunctors",
 "statement": "Let $S$ be a scheme [def-pc-scheme] and let $F$ be a sheaf of sets on $(\\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ [def-pc-fppf-site, def-weil-pbc-sheafification]. Suppose there is a set-indexed family of subfunctors $F_i\\subset F$ such that each $F_i$ is an algebraic space [def-trf-algebraic-space], each map $F_i\\to F$ is representable and an open immersion, the map $\\coprod_iF_i\\to F$ is surjective as a sheaf map, and $\\coprod_iF_i$ is an algebraic space. Then $F$ is an algebraic space.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/spaces.tex",
  "place": "Tag 02WR (glueing-algebraic-spaces), all five hypotheses and its representability/diagonal/gluing argument."
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
